      "text": "To determine when the expression \\(\\frac{y+6}{y^2 - 5y + 4}\\) is undefined, we need to identify the values of \\(y\\) that make the denominator zero. The expression is undefined when the denominator is zero because division by zero is not defined.\n\nThe denominator of the expression is \\(y^2 - 5y + 4\\). We need to solve the equation:\n\\[ y^2 - 5y + 4 = 0. \\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation, which we can factorize as follows:\n\\[ y^2 - 5y + 4 = (y - 1)(y - 4). \\]\n\nSetting each factor equal to zero gives us the solutions:\n\\[ y - 1 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y - 4 = 0, \\]\n\\[ y = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y = 4. \\]\n\nTherefore, the expression \\(\\frac{y+6}{y^2 - 5y + 4}\\) is undefined at \\(y = 1\\) and \\(y = 4\\). The sum of these values is:\n\\[ 1 + 4 = 5. \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all values of \\(y\\) for which the expression is undefined is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
